{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal","id":481988,"title":"Taking more damage when your track is full of bashing or lethal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-15T23:20:55-07:00","id":481988,"title":"Taking more damage when your track is full of bashing or lethal","content":"I'm not really sure I understand how to track the damage... on the damage track... especially if it's already full, in the particular case of vampires. I've just read this other thread (here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/221974-downgrading-damage-torpor-and-final-death/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...al-death/page2</a>) and it helped clear things up... a bit. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If, as a Vampire, your track is full of bashing (say a pool of 7, looking like: / / / / / / / ), you don't fall unconscious/incapacitated; you stay &quot;awake&quot; and suffer wound penalties (-3) to all relevant dice pools. True?</li> <li>If you suffer one more point of bashing, you swap the leftmost point of bashing on the already full damage track and convert it into a point of Lethal. Looking like: X / / / / / / ?</li> <li>If you suffer a point of Lethal instead, you do the same thing as above, meaning that contrary to a misconception (and I quote: \u00abmistakenly thinking that damage that gets pushed off the right end of the Health track wraps back around instead of being ignored\u00bb see above link), if your track is full of bashing already, additional points of Bashing or Lethal both equate to the same result. Looking like: X / / / / / / ?</li> <li>If, for some reason, your track is full of Lethal damage, and you need to keep track the amount of added damage on top (be it because you got the Eternal Frenzy Coil, Rites of the Impaled merit, or even if someone is hitting your torpid corpse to get rid of you permanently), what does adding one point of Bashing do? Does it convert a point of Lethal to Aggravated or not?</li> <li>Does adding 1 bashing damage equate to adding 1 Lethal OR 1 Aggravated at this point, in terms of end results? All resulting in: * X X X X X X ?</li> <li>Also, should I assume that, akin to #3, any added Aggravated damage on the left doesn't make the rightmost Lethal &quot;wrap back around&quot; ?</li> <li>If I'm not mistaken, one could punch a Vampire to True Death, albeit slowly. True?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> To summarize:<br /> <br /> / / / / / / / (7 Bashing, full, Vampire is still conscious, has wound penalties of -3)<br /> <br /> Add 1 Bashing:<br /> X / / / / / /<br /> <br /> Add 1 Lethal:<br /> X X / / / / /<br /> <br /> Add 6 Lethal:<br /> * X X X X X X (Vampire should be unconscious and in torpor by now, unless merits, coils, etc.)<br /> <br /> Add 1 Lethal:<br /> * * X X X X X<br /> <br /> Add 1 Bashing:<br /> * * * X X X X<br /> <br /> Add 1 Aggravated:<br /> * * * * X X X<br /> <br /> (the above three doing the same amount of damage, whatever the type)<br /> <br /> Add 3 whatever damage:<br /> * * * * * * * (True Death, dramatic ripping of the sheet, or similar ritual)<br /> <br /> Is this true?<br /> <br /> If so, Rites of the Impale's second dot and Eternal Frenzy are a lot less useful than it would seem (the first is in a playtest document for Secrets of the Covenants, Ordo Dracul the second is in the Core rulebook):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond the Pale (\u2022\u2022): Your character does not suffer torpor when her last Health box is filled<br /> with lethal damage, unless she also suffers aggravated damage equal to her Resolve. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While he is in frenzy the Dragon will not fall into torpor even if all his Health levels are filled with lethal damage. </div> </div> </div>The first means you stay out of Torpor until you take [Resolve] boxes of any damage (since they will all get converted into Aggravated once on the Track) before entering forced torpor.<br /> <br /> The second means you get to avoid falling into torpor once your track is full of Lethal, with only Final Death to stop you, which includes damage from all three types equally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any explanation/answer !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 04-16-2015, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T23:28:43-07:00","id":482042,"title":"","content":"You got it right. When your Health is full of one particular type of Damage, any additional damage becomes the next highest type of Damage. This accumulates until all your Health boxes are full of Agg, in which case your character is dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T23:57:21-07:00","id":482058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, as a Vampire, your track is full of bashing (say a pool of 7, looking like: / / / / / / / ), you don't fall unconscious/incapacitated; you stay &quot;awake&quot; and suffer wound penalties (-3) to all relevant dice pools. True?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you suffer one more point of bashing, you swap the leftmost point of bashing on the already full damage track and convert it into a point of Lethal. Looking like: X / / / / / / ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you suffer a point of Lethal instead, you do the same thing as above, meaning that contrary to a misconception (and I quote: \u00abmistakenly thinking that damage that gets pushed off the right end of the Health track wraps back around instead of being ignored\u00bb see above link), if your track is full of bashing already, additional points of Bashing or Lethal both equate to the same result. Looking like: X / / / / / / ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct (it's a little unintuitive, but that's how it works).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, for some reason, your track is full of Lethal damage, and you need to keep track the amount of added damage on top (be it because you got the Eternal Frenzy Coil, Rites of the Impaled merit, or even if someone is hitting your torpid corpse to get rid of you permanently), what does adding one point of Bashing do? Does it convert a point of Lethal to Aggravated or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it does. When your health track is full of Lethal damage, any damage of any type upgrades the leftmost box not filled with Aggravated damage from Lethal to Aggravated.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does adding 1 bashing damage equate to adding 1 Lethal OR 1 Aggravated at this point, in terms of end results? All resulting in: * X X X X X X ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, should I assume that, akin to #3, any added Aggravated damage on the left doesn't make the rightmost Lethal &quot;wrap back around&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not mistaken, one could punch a Vampire to True Death, albeit slowly. True?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though like you said it would take a long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To summarize:<br /> <br /> / / / / / / / (7 Bashing, full, Vampire is still conscious, has wound penalties of -3)<br /> <br /> Add 1 Bashing:<br /> X / / / / / /<br /> <br /> Add 1 Lethal:<br /> X X / / / / /<br /> <br /> Add 6 Lethal:<br /> * X X X X X X (Vampire should be unconscious and in torpor by now, unless merits, coils, etc.)<br /> <br /> Add 1 Lethal:<br /> * * X X X X X<br /> <br /> Add 1 Bashing:<br /> * * * X X X X<br /> <br /> Add 1 Aggravated:<br /> * * * * X X X<br /> <br /> (the above three doing the same amount of damage, whatever the type)<br /> <br /> Add 3 whatever damage:<br /> * * * * * * * (True Death, dramatic ripping of the sheet, or similar ritual)<br /> <br /> Is this true?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is exactly right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal#post481988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, Rites of the Impale's second dot and Eternal Frenzy are a lot less useful than it would seem (the first is in a playtest document for Secrets of the Covenants, Ordo Dracul the second is in the Core rulebook):<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The first means you stay out of Torpor until you take [Resolve] boxes of any damage (since they will all get converted into Aggravated once on the Track) before entering forced torpor.<br /> <br /> The second means you get to avoid falling into torpor once your track is full of Lethal, with only Final Death to stop you, which includes damage from all three types equally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any explanation/answer !</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty darn useful. Normally you would fall to Torpor as soon as your health track is full of Lethal damage. With the second dot of Rites of the Impaled (as it works currently - there's every possibility it may change by the final draft) you get to stay up until you take [Resolve] more damage. That's a pretty big deal when you think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T00:53:09-07:00","id":482113,"title":"","content":"Yup, it's gonna be useful pretty rarely (when you're almost dead), but when it does take effect, it's probably saving your life (since at that moment you're very likely to be in frenzy trying to run away for your life)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T00:59:58-07:00","id":482114,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers both !! Very much appreciated !<br /> <br /> What I meant by &quot;less useful&quot; is just that you only get a few more boxes before Final Death, which while being useful, also uncomfortably &quot;squeezes&quot; the &quot;buffer zone&quot; between torpor and Final Death. Meaning that your enemies may have to face you for a bit longer, but that in the end, if they wish to incapacitate you, they have to do so by... killing you permanently instead of the good ol' tropor K.O. All those boons are perfectly thematic, but they are much more daredevil that one could be led to believe; you're basically gambling a lot more with your (un)life versus most opponents (those that want to simply you K.O.). Of course the ones that *really* want you dead would have to fight you to the bitter end for longer...<br /> <br /> Eh, hum, does anyone have a suggestion for &quot;faking death&quot;, or more like &quot;playing dead&quot; ? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T04:48:19-07:00","id":482215,"title":"","content":"Flop to the floor. Don't move. That's pretty much all a vamp has to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T05:06:16-07:00","id":482222,"title":"","content":"Though the Blush of Life means you'll have a pulse, breathe, etc. so if you also have the Blush active you may find a Manipulation+Expression or Manipulation+Subterfuge roll to 'play dead' helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T05:20:26-07:00","id":482225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481988-taking-more-damage-when-your-track-is-full-of-bashing-or-lethal?p=482215#post482215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flop to the floor. Don't move. That's pretty much all a vamp has to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd still ask for the roll, because keeping yourself unmoving, when something is trying to murder you? When the beast is shouting at your mind &quot;run&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T05:51:06-07:00","id":482239,"title":"","content":"Oh, I just found another tricky question regarding &quot;damage tracks filled with Bashing/Lethal&quot;:<br /> <br /> Remember the Iron Skin / Bulletproof vest questions people often ask? The answer often involved setting apart the damage &quot;source&quot; (for ex.: fist giving bashing, sword giving lethal, spell giving aggravated) from it's &quot;consequences&quot; down the line (such as Iron Skin reducing the damage of a fist, but not of a sword, even if you're a vampire who takes most lethal as bashing and bulletproof vests being mostly redundant with a vampire's &quot;bulletproofness&quot;).<br /> <br /> My question is basically about tilts like Arm Wrack, or any other effect with a similar wording to this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Blah Blah Blah, Lethal damage, etc.]... <b>If aggravated damage inflicts this Tilt</b>, the character loses the<br /> use of his arm (or straight up loses his arm) permanently. </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that only a real source of aggravated damage can cause the permanent loss of a limb or that in certain circumstances, such as above, bashing or lethal resulting in &quot;net&quot; aggravated damage would also count? (...in this specific case, of course a hacksaw can also do the job...) Because bashing or lethal damage inflicted on a character with all his track already filled with X X X X X X X (for ex.) would upgrade some of those into aggravated, but is this &quot;upgraded&quot; damage also a source of aggravated under the above rule?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure there are other such instances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:09:08-07:00","id":482264,"title":"","content":"I think that's just for mortals anyway. I'm 98% sure that it also says that once a vampire heals the wound the tilt goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}